  "requirement": "The mdBook preprocessor MUST report an error when a generated evidence detail page would use the path of an existing book chapter.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The code meets the requirement and a test covers it.\n\n**Implementation.** `IndexPlan::find` in `src/index.rs` (about lines 271–292) does the following:\n- It computes each generated detail page path as `<index chapter path without extension>/<definition name>.md`.\n- It collects the paths of all existing book chapters into `existing_paths`.\n- It returns an `InvalidData` error (\"generated evidence page … conflicts with a book chapter\") if any detail path is in that set.\n\nThe caller in `src/lib.rs` (line 189) propagates that error with `?`. The preprocessor therefore reports the failure instead of silently overwriting the chapter. The check runs before `populate`, so no page is generated when there is a conflict.\n\n**Test.** `generated_detail_path_cannot_replace_a_chapter` in `src/index.rs` (around line 1115) is tagged with `{test}` for this requirement. It builds:\n- a book with an index chapter at `requirements-index.md`;\n- an existing chapter at `requirements-index/requirements.ready.md`;\n- a definition named `requirements.ready`.\n\nIt asserts that `IndexPlan::find` returns an error containing \"conflicts with a book chapter\".\n\n**Coverage gaps.** I found only minor ones.\n- Only the direct conflict case is tested. The check is a simple set-membership test, so I judge this sufficient.\n- There is no explicit test of the non-conflicting path, but the other index tests exercise it.\n- Chapters without a path (drafts) cannot conflict and are correctly skipped.",
